WEBVTT

00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:10.837
Good preparation can take you a long way, but some decisions are not
yours to make alone, and knowing who holds them saves time and

00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:12.700
protects the people affected.

00:00:12.822 --> 00:00:17.922
The Support page puts it simply: much of the time, the right
resource is enough.

00:00:18.044 --> 00:00:26.358
When a decision belongs to a person, this page helps you find the
supervisor, Equity Director or Specialist, policy owner or office

00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:27.483
who holds it.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.727
Support offers four ways in.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:37.967
Ask is a place to put a question in your own words and get a
considered answer, with its sources and its limits, without needing

00:00:37.967 --> 00:00:38.823
a meeting.

00:00:38.946 --> 00:00:45.912
The Library holds reviewed checklists, job aids, learning material
and practice guidance, searchable by topic.

00:00:46.034 --> 00:00:50.690
Explore an area of work lets you begin with the decision or task in
front of you.

00:00:50.812 --> 00:00:59.166
And Find the right person matches the work to the supervisor, Equity
Director or Specialist, policy owner or office responsible for it.

00:00:59.288 --> 00:01:02.061
That last one is our focus here.

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:06.750
Find the right person asks you to tell it what kind of work you are
doing.

00:01:06.872 --> 00:01:12.948
Under What kind of help do you need, you choose your role in this
work, the area of work, and the timing.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.881
Timing ranges from planning ahead to work that is already in use and
needs prompt attention.

00:01:19.003 --> 00:01:26.487
One request matters here: describe the work in general terms, and
leave out names, complaints and private case details.

00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:30.820
The page needs only the shape of the work to point you somewhere
useful.

00:01:31.387 --> 00:01:36.897
Next, the page asks whether the work sits within the Disability
Services Division.

00:01:37.019 --> 00:01:41.852
You can say it does, that it is outside the division, or that you
are not sure.

00:01:41.974 --> 00:01:49.726
Not being sure is a perfectly reasonable answer, and the page will
still help you find the right person or confirm which division owns

00:01:49.726 --> 00:01:50.547
the work.

00:01:50.669 --> 00:01:54.258
When your answers are in place, select Show who can help.

00:01:54.824 --> 00:01:57.371
Your results appear in two parts.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:02:04.460
First comes a place to start on your own, with timing advice and
links to review the area and find reviewed material.

00:02:04.582 --> 00:02:10.838
Then comes a list called People and offices to consider, with your
most likely starting point near the top.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.897
For a staff member, that is often your supervisor or manager.

00:02:15.019 --> 00:02:22.633
Before reaching out, confirm the named contact through the current
DHS staff directory, the intranet or your supervisor.

00:02:22.756 --> 00:02:27.589
Contact details appear only once the responsible office has
confirmed them.

00:02:28.156 --> 00:02:33.638
Further down, a practice example shows why one piece of work can
need more than one partner.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.559
A team wants a revised appointment reminder to work for the people
who receive it.

00:02:38.681 --> 00:02:43.948
Whether the message is clear is a question for the person
responsible for the communication.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:48.368
Whether people can use it calls for language and accessibility
support.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.701
Whether the process works belongs with the responsible program team.

00:02:52.823 --> 00:02:58.800
As the page says, the questions help prepare a conversation, and the
right person depends on the work.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:03.222
Some matters belong with another team from the very start.

00:03:03.344 --> 00:03:11.124
Complaints, investigations, grievances, accommodation decisions, and
discipline about a named person go to Employee Culture, Human

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:13.758
Resources, or the civil-rights channel.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.182
Questions of legal interpretation go to the policy or legal owner.

00:03:18.304 --> 00:03:25.215
And anything touching a Tribal Nation goes first to the Office of
Indian Policy or your Tribal liaison, through the separate

00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:29.361
government-to-government or Tribal relations process when it
applies.

00:03:29.483 --> 00:03:34.228
Learning on this site can inform those conversations, but it never
replaces them.

00:03:34.794 --> 00:03:37.939
Using this page commits you to nothing.

00:03:38.061 --> 00:03:43.538
Your choices stay on the page, no one is contacted, and no request
is submitted.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:50.182
It simply helps you see who holds the authority you need, so your
next conversation starts in the right place.

00:03:50.304 --> 00:03:55.404
The next time a decision feels bigger than your role, open Find the
right person.

00:03:55.527 --> 00:04:01.171
Answer the three questions in general terms, then reach out to the
first person on your list.
